# The catch-all goes FIRST.
#
# gitattributes resolves last-match-wins per attribute, so a trailing `* ...`
# silently overrides every specific rule above it. It was last, which made
# `-text` on the binary signature inert — `git check-attr` reported
# `text: auto` for it, meaning git would happily normalise line endings inside
# a signature and invalidate it. Same class of bug as everything else in this
# repo's recent history: a rule that looks applied and is not.
*      text=auto

# CI runs on Linux. Force LF so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# cannot commit CRLF into a file the runner then chokes on.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf

# Git hooks have no extension. A CRLF hook fails on Linux and macOS with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" — and it fails at push time, which
# is the worst moment to discover it.
.githooks/*  text eol=lf

# The evidence bundle. Its digests and its SSH signature are defined over LF
# bytes, so a CRLF checkout would break verification on a machine that did
# nothing wrong. `-text` on the signature keeps git from touching it at all.
.apexyard/attestation       text eol=lf
.apexyard/allowed_signers   text eol=lf
.apexyard/*.json            text eol=lf
.apexyard/*.md              text eol=lf
.apexyard/attestation.sig   -text

